# StageVerify Timekeeper (D-72)

Harness tool. Optimizes for **correctness + reliability + wall-clock + model-cost**. Never weakens D-38, D-60, D-42, D-51, D-50/D-55, D-65, D-66, or D-69.

## Auto machinery

Project hooks (`.cursor/hooks.json` → plugin runner) observe tools/shell/subagents and inject a `TIMEKEEPER` block **only on intervention**. Honor those blocks.

## Failure classes (do not use one recovery for all)

| Class | Recovery |
| --- | --- |
| product_failure | Debug product asserts |
| implementation_failure | New hypothesis; D-19 → D-50 ladder |
| verification_failure | Change verify approach or escalate ladder |
| measurement_tool_failure | Fix measurement once; else metric unavailable — do **not** invalidate green D-38/D-60/build/visual |
| ci_wait / deploy_propagation_wait | Bounded poll; never restart successful deploy |
| repo_main_drift | Material-impact check; resolve only real conflicts |

## Anti-thrash

Same operation fails twice → **STOP repeating**. Classify → change method / escalate / PARTIAL / BLOCKED.

Benchmark budget: 3–5 clean samples (median/range/confidence). Stop when the decision is clear.

## Timed checkpoints (also enforced by hooks when possible)

- ~10m no material progress → strategy checkpoint
- ~15m → status / shortest safe path
- ~25m → completion-focus (no redo of approved work / green gates)
- ~35m → choose A finish / B continue (name progress) / C PARTIAL / D BLOCKED + D-66 terminal status

## Hard non-weaken contract

Timekeeper may advise skipping **redundant unchanged reruns**. It must **never** authorize skipping a required gate that existing rules still require for the ship class.
